Package: cashr
Type: Package
Title: Empirical Bayes Normal Means with Correlated Noise
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Lei", "Sun", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "leisun2357@gmail.com"),
    person("Matthew", "Stephens", role = "aut"))
Description: Fits empirical Bayes normal means models when the noise is correlated,
    using the exchangeable correlated noise (ECN) model of Sun and Stephens
    <arXiv:1812.07488>: the realized empirical distribution of correlated N(0,1) noise
    is expanded in Gaussian derivatives and estimated jointly with the prior of the
    normal means. Provides local false discovery rates, q-values, posterior means and
    local false sign rates. The default solver is a self-contained barrier Newton
    method; the original MOSEK-based algorithm is available as an option.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/LSun/cashr
BugReports: https://github.com/LSun/cashr/issues
Depends: R (>= 3.5)
Imports: stats, graphics
Suggests: Rmosek (>= 10.0), REBayes, SQUAREM, Matrix, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
